  "verbalization": "Epi-Fibrauretinoside A is shown to have a target relationship with A2780cisR through multiple pathways, with the most consistent link being its interaction with Dual serine/threonine and tyrosine protein kinase. This kinase is identified as a target of both (3E,5R)-3-[2-[(1S,4aS,8aS)-5,5,8a-trimethyl-2-methylidene-3,4,4a,6,7,8-hexahydro-1H-naphthalen-1-yl]ethylidene]-5-hydroxyoxolan-2-one and CID 21778290, which in turn targets A2780cisR. The evidence suggests that Epi-Fibrauretinoside A may act as a modulator of this kinase, potentially influencing its activity and thereby affecting A2780cisR. The presence of multiple targets and their shared relationship with A2780cisR indicates a possible mechanism involving kinase regulation, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
